Wave 9. The tide comes in, goes out, comes in again. Theo counts them under his breath, the way his father taught him, and loses count, and starts again from one.

Wave 10. The tide comes in, goes out, comes in again. Theo counts them under his breath, the way his father taught him, and loses count, and starts again from one.

Wave 11. The tide comes in, goes out, comes in again. Theo counts them under his breath, the way his father taught him, and loses count, and starts again from one.

Wave 12. The tide comes in, goes out, comes in again. Theo counts them under his breath, the way his father taught him, and loses count, and starts again from one.

Wave 13. The tide comes in, goes out, comes in again. Theo counts them under his breath, the way his father taught him, and loses count, and starts again from one.

Wave 14. The tide comes in, goes out, comes in again. Theo counts them under his breath, the way his father taught him, and loses count, and starts again from one.

MARIE
Come. They're waiting.

THEO
Let them wait.

AUGUSTIN
The boat leaves at six. With or without either of you.

MARIE
With.

> FADE OUT.
